<title>SPAIN: Spain's Continente 1996 net 10.15 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Spain's Continente 1996 net 10.15 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full 1996 results for hypermarket chain Continente group, in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Net turnover			    440.46   vs   407.01</p>
<p> Sales margin			     61.91   vs    53.60</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			  88.47   vs    79.02</p>
<p> Operating profit			 12.32   vs    13.24</p>
<p> Pretax profit			    14.03   vs    14.69</p>
<p> Net profit				 10.15   vs    11.58</p>
<p> Operating cash flow		    23.51   vs    23.07</p>
<p>NOTE: Continente said gross turnover in 1996 was up eight percent to 485 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Sales were affected by weak family consumption, but the firm offset this with an aggressive sales policy, and managed to increase its market share in foods.</p>
<p>The firm opened three new hypermarkets in 1996, bringing the total to 48, and plans three new centres in 1997.</p>
</text>
